<title>FINLAND: ASKO SAYS LANOR'S STAKE FELL TO 19.9 PCT.</title>
<headline>ASKO SAYS LANOR'S STAKE FELL TO 19.9 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish plastic pipes, household appliances and furniture maker Asko Oy said on Thursday that Lanor Oy had reduced its stake in Asko to below 20 percent from more than 23 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Asko's second largest owner Lanor Oy ... has on March 26, 1997 lowered its stake in Asko from 23.02 percent to 19.9 percent by selling 200,000 shares,&quot; Asko said in a statement.</p>
<p>Asko did not identify the buyer.</p>
<p>Asko said it owned 47.1 percent of Lanor with Finnish oil and chemicals group Neste Oy holding 47.1 percent and insurer Sampo 5.8 percent.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
